1
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:04,598
[Leo] Ava, there are 438 items in the Atlas.

2
00:00:04,618 --> 00:00:06,089
[Leo] How do I find mine?

3
00:00:06,109 --> 00:00:07,004
[Ava] Two filters.

4
00:00:07,024 --> 00:00:09,565
[Ava] Open the Master checklist and I'll show you.

5
00:00:10,215 --> 00:00:11,716
[Ava] First, filter by wave.

6
00:00:11,736 --> 00:00:13,091
[Ava] Let's pick Wave 1.

7
00:00:13,111 --> 00:00:16,643
[Leo] Then by workstream, which is my team, Talent Acquisition.

8
00:00:16,663 --> 00:00:17,941
[Ava] Now it's a short list.

9
00:00:17,961 --> 00:00:20,294
[Ava] Open one, like Background screening.

10
00:00:20,944 --> 00:00:22,561
[Ava] Set yourself as the assignee.

11
00:00:22,581 --> 00:00:24,905
[Ava] Type your name and pick yourself from the list.

12
00:00:24,925 --> 00:00:25,549
[Leo] Done.

13
00:00:25,569 --> 00:00:26,939
[Leo] It's officially mine.

14
00:00:26,959 --> 00:00:28,248
[Leo] No take-backs.

15
00:00:28,268 --> 00:00:32,604
[Ava] Now set the status to Drafting and a target date you actually believe in.

16
00:00:32,624 --> 00:00:34,507
[Leo] Saved for everyone, instantly.

17
00:00:34,527 --> 00:00:36,907
[Leo] Goodbye, emailing the tracker around.

18
00:00:37,557 --> 00:00:41,517
[Ava] Then add a note: where the document lives, what's missing, your next step.

19
00:00:41,537 --> 00:00:43,113
[Leo] So not just "working on it"?

20
00:00:43,133 --> 00:00:45,549
[Leo] That's been my status since 2019.

21
00:00:45,569 --> 00:00:48,224
[Ava] A good note means nobody has to chase you.

22
00:00:48,874 --> 00:00:50,888
[Leo] How often do I need to do this?

23
00:00:50,908 --> 00:00:51,750
[Ava] Every week.

24
00:00:51,770 --> 00:00:54,941
[Ava] The status report is generated straight from the checklist,

25
00:00:54,961 --> 00:00:57,074
[Ava] so leadership reads what you enter.

26
00:00:57,094 --> 00:01:00,442
[Leo] Skip a week and the steering committee reads old news.

27
00:01:00,462 --> 00:01:01,461
[Leo] Got it.

28
00:01:02,111 --> 00:01:02,838
[Leo] Uh oh.

29
00:01:02,858 --> 00:01:04,268
[Leo] Why is this one red?

30
00:01:04,288 --> 00:01:08,059
[Ava] It's overdue: the target date has passed and the item isn't finished.

31
00:01:08,079 --> 00:01:10,107
[Ava] Maybe the approver's on vacation.

32
00:01:10,127 --> 00:01:10,866
[Leo] Classic.

33
00:01:10,886 --> 00:01:12,927
[Leo] So do I just quietly move the date?

34
00:01:12,947 --> 00:01:13,913
[Ava] Not quietly.

35
00:01:13,933 --> 00:01:18,446
[Ava] Note what's blocking it, agree a new date with your workstream lead, then update it.

36
00:01:19,096 --> 00:01:23,068
[Ava] Filter, open, assign yourself, update status and date, leave a note.

37
00:01:23,088 --> 00:01:24,039
[Ava] Every week.

38
00:01:24,059 --> 00:01:26,727
[Leo] A few minutes a week and nobody chases me?

39
00:01:26,747 --> 00:01:27,477
[Leo] Sold.

40
00:01:27,497 --> 00:01:30,061
[Leo] Next up, documenting a process.
